================================================================================
AUCTION SPECIFICATION - IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE (LEGACY)
================================================================================

This document contains implementation-specific details that supplement the
auction-spec. It is provided for reference when implementing or maintaining
the auction mechanism but is NOT part of the normative specification.

For the authoritative protocol specification, see auction-spec.

================================================================================
PREFIXES TO REGISTER (ON STARTUP)
================================================================================

- heartbeat SVS prefix: /<group prefix>/heartbeat
- /<node prefix>/bid
- /<node prefix>/results

================================================================================
IMPLEMENTATION CONSTANTS
================================================================================

AUCTION_TIMEOUT = 3.5 × expected max RTT

    For the testbed topology, RTT ≈ 500ms, giving AUCTION_TIMEOUT ≈ 1.75s

    This accounts for:
        T_bid     = RTT    (bid interest → peer → bid data back to auctioneer)
        T_result = RTT    (result interest → auctioneer → result data back)
        T_update = 1.5×RTT (NodeUpdate propagation to all nodes after job claim)

    Total = RTT + RTT + 1.5×RTT = 3.5×RTT

AUCTION_BACKUP_DELAY = AUCTION_TIMEOUT + 2s

    Time to wait for an earlier auction to complete and SVS to propagate
    before initiating a backup auction.

Note: These values are calibrated for the testbed topology. Other deployments
SHOULD adjust based on expected network characteristics.

================================================================================
CLI FLAGS
================================================================================

The following command-line flags control auction behavior:

    --auction-timeout duration
        Timeout for waiting for MetricResponse from peers.
        Default: 1.75s (calibrated for testbed)

    --auction-backup-delay duration
        Delay before initiating a backup auction.
        Default: 3.75s

================================================================================
AUCTION HEARTBEATS
================================================================================

The auction mechanism uses a separate SVS group for heartbeats:

    - SVS group prefix: /<group prefix>/heartbeat
    - Increase sequence number by 1 every HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL (5s)
    - Note: This does not publish any data, and nodes do not attempt to
      fetch the update

See shared-spec for additional heartbeat behavior.

================================================================================
AUCTIONEER PSEUDOCODE
================================================================================

The following pseudocode describes the auctioneer's behavior:

function runAuction(target, rf):
    timestamp = uint64(time.Now().UnixNano())
    resultsName = /<self prefix>/results/v=<timestamp>

    // Send bid interests to all peers
    for each node in peerList:
        if node == self or node.isDoing(target):
            continue
        interestName = /<node prefix>/bid/v=<timestamp>
        appParams = MetricRequest {
            Target: target,
            Timestamp: timestamp,
            ResultsName: resultsName
        }
        sendInterest(interestName, appParams)

    // Wait for responses
    responses = waitForResponses(AUCTION_TIMEOUT)

    // Check for Delay
    for each response in responses:
        if response.Delay == true:
            publishJobAssignment(resultsName, target, nil)
            return

    // Determine winners
    candidates = filter(nodes, not node.isDoing(target))
    sort(candidates, by (used/capacity) ascending)
    winners = candidates[0 : rf - currentReplication]

    // Publish results
    publishJobAssignment(resultsName, target, winners)

function publishJobAssignment(resultsName, target, assignees):
    data = JobAssignment {
        Target: target,
        Assignees: assignees
    }
    client.Store().Put(data, resultsName)

================================================================================
PEER PSEUDOCODE
================================================================================

The following pseudocode describes peer behavior when receiving a bid interest:

function onBidInterest(interest):
    request = parseMetricRequest(interest.AppParams)
    timestamp = request.Timestamp
    resultsName = request.ResultsName

    // Determine Delay
    if request.Target == currentAuctionTarget:
        if timestamp < currentAuctionTimestamp:
            delay = true              // Their auction is earlier
        elif timestamp > currentAuctionTimestamp:
            delay = false             // Our auction is earlier
        else:
            delay = (ourNodeName > request.AuctioneerName)
    else:
        delay = false  // Different target, no conflict

    // Respond with metrics
    response = MetricResponse {
        Capacity: storageCapacity,
        Used: storageUsed,
        Delay: delay
    }
    sendData(interest.Name, response)

    // Subscribe to results
    expressInterest(resultsName, onResultsData)

================================================================================
HANDLING RESULTS DATA
================================================================================

function onResultsData(data):
    assignment = parseJobAssignment(data.Content)

    if assignment.Assignees is nil or empty:
        // Auction cancelled
        if isUnderReplicated(assignment.Target):
            runAuction(assignment.Target, rf)
        return

    if ourNodeName in assignment.Assignees:
        doJob(assignment.Target)
        publishNodeUpdate()

    if isUnderReplicated(assignment.Target):
        runAuction(assignment.Target, rf)

================================================================================
PENDING ASSIGNMENT BUFFER
================================================================================

If an assignment is received before the corresponding command:

    buffer[target] = assignment

On NodeUpdate receipt with NewCommand:

    if command.Target in buffer:
        assignment = buffer[command.Target]
        if isUnderReplicated(command.Target):
            doJob(command.Target)
            delete buffer[command.Target]
            if isUnderReplicated(command.Target):
                runAuction(command.Target, rf)

================================================================================
EVENT LOGGING
================================================================================

The following events SHOULD be logged for debugging and analysis:

    auction_started     - Auction initiated for a target
    auction_cancelled  - Auction cancelled due to Delay response
    auction_bid_received - Received MetricResponse from a peer
    auction_completed   - Auction completed with winners selected
    auction_delayed    - Local auction delayed due to peer timestamp
    pending_assignment_buffered - Assignment buffered awaiting command

================================================================================
EXAMPLE: 3-NODE AUCTION FLOW
================================================================================

Topology:
    - nodeA: auctioneer (initiator)
    - nodeB: peer
    - nodeC: peer
    - Job Target: /ndn/producer/mytarget/t=1234567890
    - Replication Factor: 2

Flow:

1. nodeA detects under-replication for target
   - Generates timestamp: 1700000000123456789
   - ResultsName: /ndn/repo/nodeA/results/v=1700000000123456789

2. nodeA sends Bid Interests to nodeB, nodeC
   - Interest name: /ndn/repo/nodeB/bid/v=1700000000123456789
   - AppParams: MetricRequest {
        Target: /ndn/producer/mytarget/t=1234567890,
        Timestamp: 1700000000123456789,
        ResultsName: /ndn/repo/nodeA/results/v=1700000000123456789
      }

3. nodeB, nodeC receive Bid Interests
   - Parse MetricRequest
   - Determine Delay (based on timestamp comparison)
   - Send MetricResponse with storage metrics
   - Subscribe to ResultsName

4. nodeA receives MetricResponses
   - No Delay received
   - Determine winners (nodes with lowest storage utilization %)
   - Suppose nodeA (30% used) and nodeB (40% used) win

5. nodeA publishes JobAssignment
   - Data name: /ndn/repo/nodeA/results/v=1700000000123456789
   - Content: {
        Target: /ndn/producer/mytarget/t=1234567890,
        Assignees: [nodeA, nodeB]
      }

6. nodeB, nodeC receive JobAssignment
   - nodeB sees it's in Assignees → claims job
   - nodeC is not in Assignees → no action
   - Both check replication: satisfied (2 >= RF)

